# AULA F75 Compx 2.4G receiver (3554:fa09). The battery is read over its
# vendor pipe. Wired mode enumerates as a different device (258a:010c) that
# the helper never opens, so it is deliberately not granted access here.
#
# The receiver's hidraw nodes are root-only by default, so the helper cannot
# open them.
# uaccess hands an ACL to whoever is logged in at the active seat, which is
# narrower than the MODE="0666" that older guides suggest - that would expose
# the keyboard's raw input stream, keystrokes included, to every account on
# the machine.
#
# The 60- prefix matters. udev runs rules in lexical order and systemd's
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-uaccess.rules is what turns the tag into an ACL, so
# a file numbered above 70 sets the tag too late and silently does nothing.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3554", ATTRS{idProduct}=="fa09", TAG+="uaccess"
